### A. Earth.ts
**Location:** `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\ts\objects\shared\Earth.ts`

**Pattern:**
- Multiple texture maps (albedo, bump, specular, clouds alpha)
- `MeshStandardMaterial` for realistic rendering
- Custom shader material for atmosphere effect
- Async texture loading: `Promise.all([loadTexture(...)])`
- Shader patching via `onBeforeCompile` (injects cloud shadows)

**Key code:**
```typescript
const [albedoMap, bumpMap, oceanMap, cloudsMap] = await Promise.all([
  this._loadTexture(paths.dayTextureUrl, true),   // sRGB
  this._loadTexture(paths.bumpTextureUrl, false),
  this._loadTexture(paths.specularTextureUrl, false),
  this._loadTexture(paths.cloudsAlphaTextureUrl, false),
]);

this._earthMaterial = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
  map: albedoMap,
  bumpMap,
  bumpScale: o.bumpScale,
  roughnessMap: oceanMap,
  metalness: 0.07,
  metalnessMap: oceanMap,
});

// Custom shader injection
earthMaterial.onBeforeCompile = (shader) => {
  shader.uniforms.tClouds = { value: cloudsMap };
  shader.fragmentShader = shader.fragmentShader.replace(
    "#include <common>",
    earthPatchCommonShader,
  );
};
```

