## Summary of Patterns to Replicate

| Pattern | Used By | Example |
|---------|---------|---------|
| **Procedural Geometry** | GravityBalls, CloudPlane | CircleGeometry, PlaneGeometry + vertex manipulation |
| **Texture Maps** | Earth, Planet | map, bumpMap, metalness/roughness maps |
| **Shader Materials** | Earth (atmosphere), Planet (atmosphere), CloudPlane | Custom vertex/fragment shaders |
| **Dynamic Material Patching** | Earth | `material.onBeforeCompile` |
| **Shared Texture Cache** | CloudPlane | Static Map with ref-counting |
| **Runtime Geometry Updates** | CloudPlane | Position attribute manipulation + `needsUpdate` |
| **Async Texture Loading** | Earth, Planet, CloudPlane | `Promise.all([loadTexture(...)])` |
| **Rotation/Animation** | Earth (continuous rotation) | `rotateY()` in `runUpdate()` |
| **Parenting/Attachment** | GravityBalls, JetEngine | `attachTo` option + `getObject()` context |
| **Uniform Management** | All shader objects | `uniforms: {...}` in `ShaderMaterial` |

For your new feature, pick one or combine: procedural (like GravityBalls), texture-mapped (like Earth/Planet), or shader-driven (like CloudPlane).

